- bug_class: "Mapping Consistency"

CODE_EXCERPT:
The commitment_indices mapping and deduplication logic lives inside the external `c-kzg-4844` library (imported as `ckzg4844`), specifically in the `VerifyCellKZGProofBatch` function. In the Prysm codebase, the wrapper functions are:

```go
// beacon-chain/blockchain/kzg/kzg.go:96-106
func VerifyCellKZGProofBatch(commitmentsBytes []Bytes48, cellIndices []uint64, cells []Cell, proofsBytes []Bytes48) (bool, error) {
	ckzgCells := make([]ckzg4844.Cell, len(cells))
	for i := range cells {
		ckzgCells[i] = ckzg4844.Cell(cells[i])
	}
	return ckzg4844.VerifyCellKZGProofBatch(commitmentsBytes, cellIndices, ckzgCells, proofsBytes)
}
```

```go
// beacon-chain/blockchain/kzg/validation.go:105-165 (VerifyCellKZGProofBatchFromBlobData)
// Constructs allCommitments, allIndices, allCells, allProofs arrays and calls VerifyCellKZGProofBatch
// Each blob's commitment is replicated per column: allCommitments[i] = Bytes48(commitments[blobIndex])
// Column indices are sequential: allIndices = [0, 1, ..., numberOfColumns-1] per blob
```

```go
// beacon-chain/core/peerdas/p2p_interface.go:60-87 (VerifyDataColumnsSidecarKZGProofs)
// Aggregates from sidecars: commitments from sidecar.KzgCommitments[i], indices from sidecar.Index (repeated per column)
```

SUBGRAPH:
The commitment deduplication is a spec-level optimization inside `verify_cell_kzg_proof_batch_impl` in the c-kzg-4844 library. Prysm passes commitments directly without deduplication - it repeats the same commitment for each cell belonging to the same blob. The deduplication (grouping identical commitments and accumulating weights) happens entirely within the C library.
